.TH ADVANCE 1 "October 2026" "Universal Linux" "Update Manager"
.SH NAME
advance \- Universal system update manager with modular plugins and snapshot integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B advance
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B advance
is a modular, portable system update utility for Linux. Everything runs through configuration plugins organized into directory-based groups under \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/advance/managers.d/\fR (default: \fB~/.config/advance/managers.d/\fR).
.PP
Advance automatically resolves package managers within each group by priority, runs pre-flight network connectivity checks, coordinates transactional pre-update and post-update system snapshots via \fBcheckpoint\fR, and handles failure recovery through automatic fallback chains.
.PP
If an active package manager in a group encounters an error during updates, Advance provides an interactive retry escalation menu featuring an automatic \fBFallback\fR option to switch to the next available manager in that group.

.SH TARGETING & GROUPS
.B Groups
are defined by subdirectories inside \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/advance/managers.d/\fR (default \fB~/.config/advance/managers.d/\fR):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/advance/managers.d/
|-- system/                  (group: system)
|   |-- pacman.conf          (priority 0)
|   |-- yay.conf             (priority 10)
|   \-- paru.conf            (priority 15)
|-- flatpak/                 (group: flatpak)
|   \-- flatpak.conf         (priority 0)
|-- node/                    (group: node)
|   |-- npm.conf             (priority 0)
|   \-- pnpm.conf            (priority 10)
\-- custom.conf              (standalone / ungrouped)
.fi
.RE
.PP
Within each group, managers must have distinct priority values. Groups execute in order of their group execution priority (default: \fBsystem\fR is 100, other groups are 50, configurable via \fBadvance config\fR or \fBGROUP_PRIORITY_<group>\fR). Only the highest-priority installed and enabled manager runs as the active manager. Lower-priority managers remain on standby for fallback if the active manager fails. Loose \fB.conf\fR files in the root of \fBmanagers.d/\fR are standalone and run whenever enabled.

.SH OPTIONS
.SS Modes
.TP
.BR \-ch ", " \-\-check
Check for available updates across all active sources without installing them. Displays update counts and package totals. When combined with \fB\-v\fR/\fB\-\-verbose\fR, displays the list of upgradable packages for each source. Does not require sudo privileges.

.SS Target Selection
Specifying any target flag activates "only-mode", disabling all unselected managers and snapshot phases unless explicitly requested.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-only " \fIMANAGER\fR"
Only run updates for the specified package manager (e.g. \fBpacman\fR, \fByay\fR, \fBflatpak\fR). Repeatable. When multiple managers in the same group are specified via \fB\-\-only\fR, group competition is bypassed, force-running all of them together.
.TP
.BR \-og ", " \-\-only\-group " \fIGROUP\fR"
Only run managers belonging to the specified group (e.g. \fBsystem\fR, \fBflatpak\fR, \fBnode\fR). Repeatable. Group resolution applies, selecting the highest-priority available manager in the group.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no " \fIMANAGER\fR"
Skip updates for the specified package manager. Repeatable. If the skipped manager was the active manager in a group, Advance falls through to the next highest-priority available manager in that group.
.TP
.BR \-ng ", " \-\-no\-group " \fIGROUP\fR"
Skip an entire group of package managers. Repeatable.

.SS Phase Control
.TP
.BR \-oprs ", " \-\-only\-pre\-snapshot
Create a pre-update system snapshot only.
.TP
.BR \-ops ", " \-\-only\-post\-snapshot
Create a post-update system snapshot only.
.TP
.BR \-nprs ", " \-\-no\-pre\-snapshot
Skip creating the pre-update snapshot.
.TP
.BR \-ns ", " \-\-no\-snapshot
Skip creating the post-update snapshot.
.TP
.BR \-nc ", " \-\-no\-cleanup
Skip snapshot auto-cleanup after updates.

.SS Snapshot Modifiers
.TP
.BR \-fprs ", " \-\-force\-pre\-snapshot
Force pre-update snapshot creation, ignoring minimum age threshold and whether updates are found.
.TP
.BR \-fs ", " \-\-force\-snapshot
Force post-update snapshot creation even if no packages were upgraded.
.TP
.BR \-kprs ", " \-\-keep\-pre\-snapshot
Mark pre-update snapshot as protected \fB[KEEP]\fR.
.TP
.BR \-ks ", " \-\-keep\-snapshot
Mark post-update snapshot as protected \fB[KEEP]\fR.
.TP
.BR \-fd ", " \-\-force\-delete
Allow deletion of protected \fB[KEEP]\fR snapshots during auto-cleanup.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep " \fIN\fR"
Override snapshot retention limit (Default: 6).

.SS Update Modifiers
.TP
.BR \-ef ", " \-\-extra\-flag " \fIMANAGER:FLAG\fR"
Append an extra persistent flag to the specified package manager for this run only (e.g. \fBadvance \-ef yay:\-\-devel\fR). Repeatable across different managers or flags.
.TP
.BR \-nef ", " \-\-no\-extra\-flags " \fIMANAGER\fR"
Clear all extra flags for the specified package manager for this run only (e.g. \fBadvance \-nef yay\fR). Repeatable. Can be combined with \fB\-ef\fR to replace extra flags.
.TP
.BR \-ex ", " \-\-exclude " \fIPACKAGE\fR"
Exclude package from system package updates. Repeatable. Excluded packages are automatically mapped to the appropriate package manager flag (e.g. \fB\-\-ignore\fR for pacman/aur helpers, \fB\-\-exclude\fR for dnf, or temporary holds for apt).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Force manual confirmation mode for all managers. Strips auto-confirm flags (\fBFLAGS_AUTO_CONFIRM\fR) and appends \fBFLAGS_INTERACTIVE\fR when configured. Overrides per-manager and global auto-confirm settings.

.SS General Options
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-self\-update ", " \-\-selfupdate
Update the Advance and Checkpoint tool suite by pulling latest changes from the git repository and reinstalling.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-changelog " [" \fIVERSION\fR "]"
Display formatted release notes from the changelog. If executed interactively in a terminal without arguments and \fBfzf\fR is available, launches an interactive version browser.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose ", " \-\-debug
Enable detailed debug logs.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage and options.

.SS Subcommands
.TP
.B changelog \fR[\fIVERSION\fR]
Browse interactive release history or print formatted release notes for a specific version (or \fB\-\-latest\fR).
.TP
.B config
Open the interactive configuration menu (requires \fBfzf\fR), including visual group & manager priority ordering (with \fBAlt+Up\fR/\fBAlt+Down\fR reordering hotkeys and automatic conflict-free renumbering), guided package manager creation, non-destructive flag editing, and general preferences.
.TP
.B config export \fR[\fIMANAGER\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR]
Print configuration for the specified manager to stdout, or bundle all manager configurations into a tarball (\fBadvance-managers.tar.gz\fR).
.TP
.B config import \fI<file|url>\fR
Import manager configuration(s) from a local \fB.conf\fR file, a tarball bundle, or a remote URL.
.TP
.B schedule
Open the interactive systemd auto-update scheduling wizard.
.TP
.B catalog \fR[\fBlist\fR|\fBscan\fR|\fBenroll \fIMGR\fR|\fBremove \fIMGR\fR]
Manage official catalog recipes. \fBlist\fR displays all catalog recipes with installation and enrollment status; \fBscan\fR auto-enrolls all detected tools; \fBenroll\fR symlinks a catalog recipe into active managers; \fBremove\fR disables an active manager.
.TP
.BR self\-update ", " selfupdate
Pull latest changes from the git repository and reinstall the tool suite.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
Advance follows the XDG Base Directory specification. Set these variables to relocate its files:
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for configuration (default: \fB~/.config\fR). Advance uses \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/advance/\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for data (default: \fB~/.local/share\fR). Advance uses \fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/advance/\fR for its catalog and per-user libraries.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for persistent state (default: \fB~/.local/state\fR). Dismissed tips are stored in \fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/advance/dismissed_messages\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for cache data (default: \fB~/.cache\fR). Catalog probe results are stored in \fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME/advance/\fR.
.TP
.B ADVANCE_CONFIG_DIR, ADVANCE_DATA_DIR, ADVANCE_STATE_DIR, ADVANCE_CACHE_DIR
Override the corresponding Advance directory directly.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, disables ANSI colors.

.SH CONFIGURATION FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/advance/config
Main configuration file in \fBKEY=VALUE\fR format (default \fB~/.config/advance/config\fR). Managed via \fBadvance config\fR. Key settings include \fBAUTO_CONFIRM\fR (global auto-confirm default), \fBGROUP_PRIORITY_<name>\fR (integer group execution priority; higher value runs first), and \fBSKIP_CHECKPOINT_WARNING\fR (suppress prompt when Checkpoint is not installed).
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/advance/excludes
List of package names to exclude from system updates (one package name per line, comments starting with \fB#\fR ignored).
.TP
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME/advance/catalog/managers/
Official upstream catalog recipes organized by category (\fBsystem\fR, \fBflatpak\fR, \fBsnap\fR, \fBbrew\fR, \fBnode\fR, \fBrust\fR, \fBpython\fR, \fBhardware\fR). System packages install this under \fB/usr/share/advance/catalog/managers/\fR.
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/advance/managers.d/<group>/<manager>.conf
Active enrolled manager configurations or symlinks pointing to official catalog recipes.
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/advance/overrides.d/<manager>.conf
Optional user drop-in override files. Values defined here take precedence over catalog files without modifying upstream recipes. Supported fields:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNAME\fR: Display name.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEMOJI\fR: Graphical icon for UI display.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBREQUIRES_CMD\fR: Required executable binary; manager is silently skipped if not found in PATH.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPRIORITY\fR: Integer priority within the group (higher value = preferred). Must be unique per group.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCHECK_CMD\fR: Command to check for updates (leave empty to always run).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUPDATE_CMD\fR: Command to perform package updates.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFLAGS\fR: Persistent flags always appended to update command (e.g. \fB\-\-needed \-\-devel\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAUTO_CONFIRM\fR: Confirmation mode: \fBtrue\fR (ON unless forced), \fBfalse\fR (OFF unless forced), or empty (follow global setting).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFLAGS_AUTO_CONFIRM\fR: Non-interactive confirmation flag appended by default in auto-confirm mode.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFLAGS_INTERACTIVE\fR: Flag appended when running in \fB\-\-interactive\fR mode.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFLAGS_OVERRIDE\fR: Flag appended during retry escalation to force past file conflicts.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCOLOR_FLAG\fR: Color output flag appended to check and update commands when color is enabled (e.g. \fB\-\-color=always\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEXCLUDE_FLAG\fR: Flag used to exclude packages (e.g. \fB\-\-ignore\fR, \fB\-\-exclude\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEXCLUDE_JOIN\fR: How multiple excluded packages are joined: \fBcomma\fR or \fBrepeat\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEXCLUDE_HOLD_CMD\fR: Command template to hold packages before update (e.g. \fBapt\-mark hold $PKG\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEXCLUDE_UNHOLD_CMD\fR: Command template to unhold packages after update (e.g. \fBapt\-mark unhold $PKG\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCHECK_UPDATES_EXIT_CODE\fR: Exit code indicating updates are available (\fB0\fR or \fB100\fR, default \fB0\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCHECK_FILTER_PATTERN\fR: Optional regex filter pattern applied to check command output.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCHECK_TIMEOUT_FALLBACK\fR: Fallback command executed if check command times out.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCHECK_DEP_BIN\fR: Optional helper executable binary required to survey updates (e.g. \fBcheckupdates\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCHECK_DEP_INSTALL_CMD\fR: Command to automatically install the check helper if missing.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPOST_UPDATE_MSG_ID\fR: Dismissible message identifier for post-update advice.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPOST_UPDATE_MSG\fR: Advice message text shown when this manager successfully updates packages.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBENABLED\fR: Set to \fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse\fR.
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR checkpoint (1),
.BR snapper (8),
.BR timeshift (1)
